  <div class="section-label">The State Environmental Study Process</div>
  <h2>State Environmental Study: Current Status</h2>

  <p>The transition of SR-177 into Weber County is currently managed through a State Environmental Study — a rigorous analytical process designed to evaluate the physical, biological, and social impacts of the proposed extension. As of Spring 2026, the study has moved from the initial scoping phase into the <strong>Alternatives Development and Evaluation</strong> stage.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %}</p>

  <p>This stage determines the precise alignment of the "Build Alternative" and the configuration of the 4000 South terminus. Local officials have indicated UDOT is studying an alignment along 5100 West; UDOT has not published a preferred alternative.{% cite "whc-warnke-minutes" %}</p>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <p><strong>Important caveat:</strong> No preferred alignment has been officially published by UDOT as of April 2026. The State Environmental Study is still in the alternatives evaluation phase. "Settled on" language from local officials should be treated as indicative, not definitive, until UDOT publishes formal alignment maps.</p>
  </div>

